msgctxt "#30087"
msgid "Enabling this will allow pressing / quickly alternating / holding both left and right (or up and down) directions at the same time. This may cause movement-based glitches."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30088"
msgid "Show Light Gun Settings"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30089"
msgid "Enable configuration of Super Scope / Justifier / M.A.C.S. rifle input. NOTE: Quick Menu must be toggled for this setting to take effect."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30090"
msgid "Run the audio pipeline at 44.1 kHz when an MSU-1 game is loaded. When disabled, MSU-1's 44.1 kHz PCM stream is decimated to the SNES's native ~32 kHz output with no anti-alias filtering, folding the track's top octave into the audible band as slight hiss. When enabled, the MSU-1 stream passes through bit-exactly and the SPC sound is upsampled cleanly. Has no effect on non-MSU-1 games. Changing this takes effect on the next content load."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30091"
msgid "Show Advanced Audio/Video Settings"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30092"
msgid "Enable configuration of low-level video layer / GFX effect / audio channel parameters. NOTE: Quick Menu must be toggled for this setting to take effect."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30093"
msgid "Emulation Hacks"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30094"
msgid "Configure processor overclocking and emulation accuracy parameters affecting low-level performance and compatibility."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30095"
msgid "SuperFX coprocessor frequency multiplier. Can improve frame rate or cause timing errors. Values under 100% can improve game performance on slow devices."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30096"
msgid "'Compatibility' runs the GSU with snes9x2010's field-tested per-line budget. 'Hardware-derived' charges each instruction its approximate real GSU cycle cost (cache-aware fetches, 5-cycle memory accesses, amortized plot flushes), matching ares/MiSTer wait states; backported from mainline Snes9x. More accurate, less field-tested. Works together with SuperFX Overclocking."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30097"
msgid "Compatibility (snes9x2010)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30098"
msgid "Hardware-derived"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30099"
msgid "Overclock SNES CPU. May cause games to crash! Use 'Light' for shorter loading times, 'Compatible' for most games exhibiting slowdown and 'Max' only if absolutely required (Gradius 3, Super R-type...)."
msgstr ""

